WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.556 --> 00:00:16.479
Zann felt dizzy as he and his friends tumbled through the vortex.

2
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.721
Lights flashed and strange worlds passed by.

3
00:00:21.361 --> 00:00:25.242
Slowly he reached into his pocket and pulled out the guidelink.

4
00:00:25.262 --> 00:00:27.262
"Give me that!"

5
00:00:27.562 --> 00:00:30.663
Perda called over the whooshing sound of the vortex.

6
00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:32.844
"I think I can make it work."

7
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.281
"I hope you're right!"

8
00:00:35.561 --> 00:00:37.602
Zann placed the device in her hand.

9
00:00:38.582 --> 00:00:42.984
He wished he'd paid more attention when his parents were explaining the device's abilities.

10
00:00:43.884 --> 00:00:45.385
Perda fiddled with the guidelink.

11
00:00:45.405 --> 00:00:47.286
"What are you doing?"

12
00:00:47.626 --> 00:00:48.446
Gliss asked her.

13
00:00:48.466 --> 00:00:52.368
"I'm supposed to rub it to create friction," Perda said.

14
00:00:52.388 --> 00:00:56.109
"Then I focus on what type of magic I want it to find.

15
00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:00.991
It should pull us toward any world nearby that matches my thoughts."

16
00:01:02.172 --> 00:01:02.812
She frowned.

17
00:01:02.964 --> 00:01:05.266
"But so far nothing is happening!"

18
00:01:05.286 --> 00:01:08.008
"You have to figure it out!"

19
00:01:08.128 --> 00:01:09.469
Gliss sounded frantic.

20
00:01:09.489 --> 00:01:15.753
"Otherwise we could end up flying through the vortex forever!"

21
00:01:16.273 --> 00:01:21.077
Suddenly Perda swerved toward one of the wormholes, dragging her friends with her.

22
00:01:23.539 --> 00:01:25.620
Zann grabbed the wormhole's edge.

23
00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.944
Instantly the wormhole pulled them in and spat them out on the other side.

24
00:01:31.944 --> 00:01:36.888
Zann held his breath, expecting to splash into the stormy waters of Skellia.

25
00:01:37.988 --> 00:01:40.510
Instead he landed on wet ground.

26
00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.231
"Oof!" he blurted out.

27
00:01:43.392 --> 00:01:45.193
Gliss sat up and rubbed her head.

28
00:01:45.213 --> 00:01:47.095
"Ouch," she said.

29
00:01:47.715 --> 00:01:49.116
Then she looked around.

30
00:01:49.136 --> 00:01:51.578
"Hey, this isn't Skellia."

31
00:01:52.719 --> 00:01:56.241
"Not unless the oceans disappeared since we were here," Darb said.

32
00:01:57.162 --> 00:01:59.964
The world they'd landed in looked similar to Magica.

33
00:02:00.768 --> 00:02:06.693
They were in a forest clearing, with tall trees shading the light of a bright orange sun.

34
00:02:07.614 --> 00:02:11.977
Birds swooped overhead, and an insect buzzed in the grass nearby.

35
00:02:11.997 --> 00:02:15.260
"Oh well."

36
00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:16.861
Perda sighed.

37
00:02:16.881 --> 00:02:20.484
"I guess I'm still figuring out how the guidelink works."

38
00:02:20.504 --> 00:02:24.527
"At least this world looks nice and peaceful."

39
00:02:25.008 --> 00:02:26.149
Gliss peered around.

40
00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:30.072
Then she wrinkled her nose and looked down.

41
00:02:31.244 --> 00:02:33.625
"It's kind of soggy right here though.

42
00:02:34.025 --> 00:02:36.946
Let's find a drier spot to rest and regain our energy."

43
00:02:38.046 --> 00:02:38.846
Zann nodded.

44
00:02:39.346 --> 00:02:42.687
It took a lot of energy just to stay conscious in the vortex.

45
00:02:43.688 --> 00:02:46.369
They usually had to rest before they could travel again.

46
00:02:46.389 --> 00:02:49.830
"Wait! Don't go anywhere yet," Darb said.

47
00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:54.891
"We need to pay attention to landmarks so we can return to the wormhole when we're ready."

48
00:02:55.771 --> 00:02:57.832
"Oops. Good point," Zann said.

49
00:02:58.248 --> 00:03:02.650
As usual, the wormhole had spun shut as soon as they'd moved away from it.

50
00:03:03.651 --> 00:03:07.133
Now it was only visible as a tiny ripple in the air.

51
00:03:08.093 --> 00:03:11.215
If Zann hadn't known it was there, he wouldn't even have noticed it.

52
00:03:11.235 --> 00:03:16.978
"I see a crooked tree over there, and some blue flowers," Gliss said.

53
00:03:16.998 --> 00:03:19.039
"Good," Perda said.

54
00:03:19.059 --> 00:03:21.721
"We'll definitely be able to spot that tree again.

55
00:03:22.421 --> 00:03:23.462
Now let's go uphill.

56
00:03:23.742 --> 00:03:24.862
It should be dry there."

57
00:03:25.963 --> 00:03:27.804
She led the way up a gentle slope.

58
00:03:28.636 --> 00:03:30.638
Soon they reached a sunny clearing.

59
00:03:31.018 --> 00:03:34.141
Zann flopped onto the dry ground and looked at Perda.

60
00:03:34.161 --> 00:03:36.923
"So why didn't the guidelink work?"

61
00:03:37.204 --> 00:03:37.624
he asked.

62
00:03:38.725 --> 00:03:40.767
She shrugged and sat down beside him.

63
00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:43.989
"I think I know what I did wrong," she said.

64
00:03:44.009 --> 00:03:50.555
"I was focusing on the gulpers from Skellia, since they probably have the most magic on that world.

65
00:03:50.975 --> 00:03:55.980
But when Gliss said the thing about flying through the vortex, I thought about birds."

66
00:03:57.248 --> 00:04:01.689
Darb watched a bright purple bird land nearby and peck at some yellow flowers.

67
00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:05.290
"There definitely are a lot of birds here," he said.

68
00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.731
"Maybe they're the source of this world's magic."

69
00:04:07.751 --> 00:04:10.332
"They could be," Zann agreed.

70
00:04:10.772 --> 00:04:11.992
Then he frowned.

71
00:04:12.012 --> 00:04:14.953
"Uh-oh. Do you think our magic will work here?"

72
00:04:14.973 --> 00:04:19.774
"I hope so, or we won't be able to open the wormhole!"

73
00:04:20.395 --> 00:04:21.835
Gliss' eyes widened.

74
00:04:21.855 --> 00:04:23.315
"We'd better test it.

75
00:04:23.815 --> 00:04:25.396
I'll conjure us something to drink."

76
00:04:26.016 --> 00:04:27.157
She snapped her fingers.

77
00:04:27.657 --> 00:04:31.880
Blink! Zann felt a sudden surge of magic energy.

78
00:04:33.101 --> 00:04:36.403
At the same time, the entire landscape around them changed!

79
00:04:36.704 --> 00:04:38.585
The sunny meadow had disappeared.

80
00:04:39.726 --> 00:04:42.608
They were now sitting in the shade of several large trees.

81
00:04:43.588 --> 00:04:49.212
A small flock of multicolored birds perched on a squat shrub with shiny blue leaves.

82
00:04:50.813 --> 00:04:53.135
Zann gasped and jumped to his feet.

83
00:04:53.155 --> 00:04:54.156
"What happened?

84
00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.381
Did we accidentally zap somewhere else?"

85
00:04:56.401 --> 00:04:58.522
"I don't think so."

86
00:04:58.802 --> 00:04:59.822
Darb looked around.

87
00:04:59.842 --> 00:05:01.343
"We're still on a hill.

88
00:05:01.963 --> 00:05:04.184
And the position of the sun hasn't changed.

89
00:05:05.184 --> 00:05:06.865
I think we're in the same exact spot."

90
00:05:06.885 --> 00:05:10.627
"But everything around us looks different!"

91
00:05:10.867 --> 00:05:11.427
Perda said.

92
00:05:11.447 --> 00:05:17.869
"The trees, the birds "That must be how magic works in this world," Darb said.

93
00:05:17.889 --> 00:05:21.031
"Gliss' magic friction changed the landscape around us."

94
00:05:22.251 --> 00:05:23.972
"Yeah." Zann gulped.

95
00:05:24.604 --> 00:05:27.185
"I wonder if it made that crooked tree move around too.

96
00:05:27.645 --> 00:05:29.946
We might not be able to find the wormhole without it."

97
00:05:31.027 --> 00:05:32.647
"Oh no," Gliss said.

98
00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:34.628
"What about the wormhole itself?

99
00:05:35.328 --> 00:05:36.349
What if it moved?

100
00:05:37.149 --> 00:05:38.330
What if it's gone?"

101
00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.091
Perda held up the guidelink.

102
00:05:41.111 --> 00:05:45.673
"This is supposed to be able to locate strong sources of magic, right?

103
00:05:46.413 --> 00:05:48.414
Maybe it can lead us back to the wormhole."

104
00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:51.035
"Do you know how to make it do that?"

105
00:05:51.315 --> 00:05:51.955
Darb asked.

106
00:05:53.116 --> 00:05:54.945
"No." Perda bit her lip.

107
00:05:54.965 --> 00:05:56.505
"But I'll figure it out."

108
00:05:57.606 --> 00:05:58.807
She rubbed the guidelink.

109
00:05:59.407 --> 00:06:02.248
Blink! The landscape changed again.

110
00:06:02.769 --> 00:06:06.671
Now the kids found themselves standing among bushes with spiky leaves.

111
00:06:07.611 --> 00:06:13.595
Nearby several large, six-legged creatures with shaggy fur sniffed around in the grass.

112
00:06:13.615 --> 00:06:16.156
"Hmm," Perda said.

113
00:06:16.596 --> 00:06:18.057
She rubbed the guidelink again.

114
00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:23.500
Blink! Now a deep, tangled forest surrounded the kids.

115
00:06:25.452 --> 00:06:28.393
Blink! Again the scenery changed.

116
00:06:28.953 --> 00:06:30.654
Now the open meadow was back.

117
00:06:31.655 --> 00:06:37.377
But instead of birds, there was a swarm of large insects buzzing around a tree with purple bark.

118
00:06:38.457 --> 00:06:41.559
"Stop!" Gliss grabbed the guidelink out of Perda's hand.

119
00:06:41.579 --> 00:06:45.480
"Every time you create friction, the landscape changes!"

120
00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.781
"Sorry." Perda looked nervous.

121
00:06:49.962 --> 00:06:51.242
Zann knew how she felt.

122
00:06:51.743 --> 00:06:56.480
It seemed like they couldn't use magic in this world at all—not without getting lost.

123
00:06:57.504 --> 00:07:01.035
So how were they going to find their way back to the wormhole?
